data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":", \"content\": \"# QA verification report — d002 — Colour Greeting vs DESIGN.md\\n\\n**Verdict: PASS — every requirement in DESIGN.md verified; no failures found.**\\n\\nSubject: `refs/campaign/orchestrator` at commit `871270f8cdbb4086ab610c31700964e820b5f1d3`\\n(\\\"Implement Colour Greeting page per DESIGN.md\\\"), checked out detached in `~/hello-app`.\\n\\n## What I ran\\n\\n1. `git checkout refs/campaign/orchestrator` — ref present at the commit named in d002.\\n2. Static review of `DESIGN.md`, `package.json`, `index.html`, `vite.config.js`,\\n   `src/App.jsx`, `src/main.jsx`, `src/index.css`.\\n3. `grep -rniE '#[0-9a-f]{3,8}\\\\b'` over `src/`, `index.html`, `vite.config.js`,\\n   `package.json` → no hex values anywhere in the application source.\\n4. `npm install` (clean; audit advisories only, not blocking), then the documented\\n   `npm run build` → vite build succeeded (1746 modules, `dist/` produced).\\n5. The documented `npm run serve` (`vite preview`) → served at `http://localhost:4173/`\\n   (URL read from its own output), HTTP 200.\\n6. Headless Chromium (`/usr/bin/chromium-browser`) driven by `playwright-core`\\n   (isolated harness in `/tmp/opencode/qa-verify/verify.mjs`) against the served\\n   production build: DOM inspection, computed styles, real button clicks, and\\n   layout geometry measurements.\\n\\n## What I observed (each measured, not assumed)\\n\\n### Interface vs design — all pass\\n\\n| Requirement | Evidence | Result |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Exact greeting `Hello, world!` as a single `h1` | Rendered DOM: one `h1`, textContent `\\\"Hello, world!\\\"` | PASS |\\n| Three buttons labelled Blue, Orange, Violet | Rendered buttons' text: `[\\\"Blue\\\", \\\"Orange\\\", \\\"Violet\\\"]` | PASS |\\n| Default on load is Blue (`--color-cat-1`) | Computed `h1` color on load: `rgb(111,147,201)` = `#6f93c9` = the stylesheet's `--color-cat-1` value | PASS |\\n| Click Blue → `--color-cat-1` | After clicking \\\"Blue\\\": `rgb(111,147,201)` = `#6f93c9` | PASS |\\n| Click Orange → `--color-cat-6` | After clicking \\\"Orange\\\": `rgb(216,146,89)` = `#d89259` = `--color-cat-6` | PASS |\\n| Click Violet → `--color-cat-5` | After clicking \\\"Violet\\\": `rgb(158,144,204)` = `#9e90cc` = `--color-cat-5` | PASS |\\n| Header title \\\"Colour Greeting\\\", no nav | Header text is exactly \\\"Colour Greeting\\\". The design-system Header renders an internal empty `\u003cnav\u003e` skeleton (one empty `div`, zero links, zero text); the app passes no nav items (`"},"index":0}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793343986,"id":"chatcmpl-12c6ce20","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

